    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1179">

                <pb facs="1087" n="829" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg829"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111Ei9/22</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Peters</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the</hi>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Counselor for the Department of State</hi>
                    
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Lansing</hi>: Mr.
                        Hamilton, the collector of customs, at Norfolk, has
                    telephoned me that he is in receipt of the following letter from the commander
                    of the <hi rendition="#italic">Prinz Eitel Friedrich</hi>, and requests to be
                    instructed:</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p rendition="#right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 29, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Hamilton</hi>: I have up to now received
                        from you no information concerning the departure of any non-neutral vessels.
                        I hold myself therefore concerning <pb facs="1088" n="830" xml:id="pg830"/>
                        this point justified to sail at any time. I must necessarily in consequence
                        of your demand according to Hague Convention XIII, Article 16, demand timely
                        information concerning outgoing non-neutral vessels.</p>
                    <p>With the highest respect,</p>
                    <p rendition="#right">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thierichens</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Captain Commandant</hi>
                    </p>
                </quote>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. J. Peters</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
